YNYBPTMNW....

I had a very annoying Nethack dream last night. I dreamt I was playing
a very low-level wizard (only about 30 max hp or so) and I was
exploring the mines. All of a sudden I fell through a trapdoor into
this much lower level which I had never seen before. It was a little
like Orcus town - lots of floor space, little rooms off of the main
area, no tunnels. And it had tons of loot - one room had gold covering
the entire floor. On the other side of the level was an area with
spellbook after spellbook. But all this was pretty useless, because the
main thing that it had were monsters. *Really* high-level monsters -
like dragons and liches and gargoyles and so forth, all over the place.
And there was no way I could take even one of them on - my armor class
was pathetic and I think I'd forgotten my main offensive spells.

So, anyway, I spent the next hour of my dream fleeing from one pack of
monsters after another, all over the level. I was just desperate to get
*out* of there - but I couldn't find the upstair! The entire level was
unlit, which made things even worse, and it seemed like no matter where
I moved, I ran into a new bunch of monsters. I tried zapping my wand of
wishing, but my luck must have been rotten, because it didn't do
anything. Eventually I found myself trapped between two dragons and
decided I'd had it - I was just going to let them kill me. So I just
pressed the spacebar. My hitpoints dropped to 3 out of 30.

Then, a miracle occurred. Lightning streaked down from heaven,
completely destroying the monsters all around me! (It showed up as
bright blue streaks on the computer screen in my dream. Really cool.)
It gave me enough time to get away and regain some of my lost
hitpoints. Soon enough, though, I was surrounded by monsters again. The
blue lightning got most of them - except for a lich and a blue dragon.
And more monsters just kept coming. And I *still* couldn't find the
upstair!

At this point my alarm clock woke me up, and I got up, feeling totally
unrested. I really hate dreams like that -- that just drag on and on
and never end.

Anyway, at least it sparked a YANI. During a successful prayer,
undertaken during combat (i.e. you have a monster in the adjacent
square trying to hit you), if your hitpoints are at the point where
your god would ordinarily heal you, there should be a chance that your
god does *not* heal you, but instead destroys your enemy with a massive
lightning bolt (of the type used to punish you for praying too much.)
Why should only enemy priests get the advantage of their god's direct
protection?

Artemis the Ranger


